## What is bound into H3, and which decisions can invalidate it (verified in the code and manifests, 2026-10-13)
**Chain.** The Step 9 evidence file (H3) names `build_manifest_sha256` = SHA-256 of `step8_build_7a6bbe465c66/manifest.json` (gate, `s10_runner.py` line 139) plus the worksheet hash, coverage, adjudication and the two dates. That manifest binds: the spec file hash (`d5fcffadd104...`), the FZ-v1 REGISTER canonical hash (`c7d50e115b08...`, the register object only), the Step 7 freeze manifest hash (`202979de2a88...`), the SHA-256 of 15 generator-code files (`implementation_a/impl_a.py`, the 11 Step 7 freeze-set files incl. `s7_recode.py`, `s7_bundle.py`, `s7_decision.py`, the codebook, `step8/s8_build.py`, `s8_construct.py`, `s8_gates.py`) and the inventory of 2,026 published files (main/pilot prompts, checker bundles, mapping, gate report, prompt table, registry). Not bound: `step9/*`, `step10/*` (runner, scoring, analysis), the authorization template, and the official decision record (the Step 7 manifest names it only by path and entry numbers, so appending an entry changes nothing in the chain).
**A change to ANY bound item changes the manifest hash and makes an already-created H3 invalid.** Decisions that can do that, in order of likelihood:
| Decision | Changes a bound item only if | Needed before H3 |
|---|---|---|
| MD-03 K2 | always (`s7_recode.py`, codebook 5.1/5.3, new Step 7 manifest) | yes; K1 changes nothing |
| H4 rehearsal findings | the advisor decides on a new codebook version before the FZ hash (codebook is bound) | yes: finish H4 and the advisor's decision on its disagreements first |
| MD-05 PG11b narrowing | always (`s7_bundle.py`, spec 8.2 amendment = new methodology version) | yes; "keep literal" changes nothing |
| MD-05 PG3 strict reading | always (rebuild of steps 3-9: the registry and the checker bundle change, so **H1 itself is invalid**) | decide before H1 is started; "ratify" changes nothing |
| MD-05 SF/UNP Policy 1/2/parse-first | always (spec 18.2 amendment, Step 7 items) | yes; "interim" changes nothing |
| MD-10 amendment of a Step 8 choice (F-4, PG4, PG11a bundle, A6b) or I-6 turned into a gate | always (`step8/s8_*.py` and/or the 624-file projection) | yes; "confirm" changes nothing |
| MD-07 with a changed `timeout_s` or other register value | only if a register VALUE changes (a meaning clarification does not) | yes in that case |
| Any decision implemented as an edit of the spec or of the FZ-v1 register instead of a record entry (for example resolving "PENDING PRD-5" or "PENDING PRD-6" in the spec text) | always (spec hash / register hash) | yes: record the decision in the decision record, do not edit the spec |
| PRD-5 | not bound, but the evaluation tool's unit sets must be settled before the FIRST evaluation run, otherwise the evaluation has to be rerun | yes (before evaluating) |
Not able to change H3: MD-01, MD-02, MD-04, MD-06, MD-08, MD-09, E-1, Q5, Q9, P7, P11, P12 (they touch only `step10/*`, templates, new files or documents; L-C would bind two Step 10 files in the FZ index, not in the manifest).
**If K2, a narrowed PG11b or a codebook revision is adopted, the authorized sequence is:** (1) the formal decision and box R-7 (Step 7 re-freeze); (2) back up the affected Step 7 files and both manifests; (3) edit the files and run the Step 7 tests; (4) write a NEW Step 7 freeze manifest (the old one stays; `reproduce/make_step7_freeze_manifest.py` writes a new path only); (5) rebuild Step 8 with `step8/s8_build.py --out <NEW parent folder>` (the build folder is named by the registry hash, so an unchanged registry reuses the name and the tool refuses an existing target, exit 3); (6) `s8_verify.py`, `impl_b.py`, `test_impl_b.py` and the slow Step 8 suite on the new build; (7) compare the new manifest `inventory` with the old: every one of the 2,026 file hashes must be identical (then the registry, prompts and checker bundle are unchanged and a blind check already performed on the bundle stays valid); only the changed generator-code hashes and `step7_freeze_manifest_sha256` may differ; (8) record, in the closeout report, the old and new values of: Step 7 manifest sha (old `202979de2a88`), Step 8 manifest sha (old `09eed00eeb79`), each changed file (old `s7_recode.py` `ec8f948e6209`, codebook `25a74353be54`, `s7_bundle.py` `10567178b209`), spec `d5fcffadd104` and register `c7d50e115b08` (expected unchanged), and the inventory comparison result; (9) update every reference to the build path or manifest hash (gate `--build`, checklist T1, runbook); (10) only then create H3 against the NEW manifest. Any inventory difference means the registry changed: H1 must be redone. None of this is authorized yet; nothing frozen was modified.

## Response guide: what to return (and what happens if you reject or condition something)
Return ONE of: a dated copy of this file with the boxes ticked by you, or the official record entry stating each decision (model: `PROPOSED_RECORD_CORRECTION_12_37.md` section 7). It must contain:
1. For PRD-5 and MD-01..MD-10: APPROVE, REJECT or AMEND (with the amended text), and any condition or limitation. **A blank box or silence is not consent**: the entry stays PENDING and every dependent patch stays inactive.
2. MD-04: "FZ file list = L-__" (or your own paths) and "A-2 = include / exclude"; if L-C, the supplement rule.
3. MD-06: "B-1 = (a)", "(b)" or "(c)" with the disposition rule of that option.
4. The boxes **E-1, Q5, Q9, R-7, P7, P11, P12** one by one, and Q7, Q8.
5. The pilot authorization file (H5), a NEW file written by you: `authorized_by` = `owner`, `scope` = `pilot_round_1`, `max_calls` = 18, `cost_ceiling_usd` = 100, `input_tokens_per_call_assumed` (positive integer, your assumption), `max_input_characters` (positive integer, at least the longest planned prompt, 1,016). The gate reads only these fields, plus the Step 9 evidence file, a verified build and the expected register settings. Provider-related permissions are NOT read by the gate: a connection test (P11) needs its own written authorization file; a provider token count (O2) needs its own written authorization with a spending basis; the pilot itself needs your separate explicit instruction after the gate prints "gates open". The API key must be present in the environment variable (the preflight checks presence and never prints it).
6. Your name, role, the date, and the advisor's where required. The assistant fills none of it.
| If you reject or condition | What stops (stays inactive) | Documented consequence |
|---|---|---|
| PRD-5 | the trust in any blind-check evaluation | the older global unit list would need a change to `s9_blindcheck.py` and a re-verification before H1 is evaluated |
| MD-01 | the counting/SF2 rule in force | the working decision must be replaced by your choice (A1/A2a diff or another rule) and the tests rewritten; the FZ hash waits |
| MD-02 | the preflight limit and the authorization values | the template value and tests change to your limit; P3b only if Q9 |
| MD-03 K2 rejected (K1 chosen) | P4 | no code; the departure from spec line 1002 is recorded |
| MD-04 | P5, the FZ hash | no FZ hash exists, so the first pilot call is not allowed (spec 797) |
| E-1 | FZ-hash enforcement in the gates | the hash exists but is not machine-enforced; a documented weaker control |
| MD-06 / B-1 (c) | P2 | anomalies are only counted and reported; no round question |
| Q5 | the adapter field | the present inference stays; the rare shape stays SF4 (soft), documented as a limitation |
| Q9 | P3b | the assumed-token value stays unenforced |
| R-7 | Step 7 re-freeze | MD-03 K2 cannot be applied |
| P7 | the runner's anchor check | the anchor is a manual procedure |
| P11 | the connection test | L1-L5 stay UNKNOWN; the first live contact is the pilot, protected only by MD-06 if adopted |
| P12 | the O4 script | the main-run token basis must be O2 or an owner entry accepting the assumption |
| MD-05, MD-07, MD-10 | the FZ hash | each is a prerequisite of the official hash; a rejected item is reopened first |
| MD-08, MD-09 | P8, the decision script | no resume; no decision script, hence no main run |
If you add a condition, write it in the entry; the assistant will stop the dependent patch, document the consequence in the closeout report and will not apply a patch that conflicts with the condition.

## Order by critical path (what blocks what)
1. MD-05 item PRD-5 (blocks the evaluation of the human blind check) -> 1b. **everything bound into H3 before the evidence file H3 is created**: MD-03, the PG3/PG11b/SF-UNP items of MD-05, MD-10, the H4 findings (a codebook revision), and MD-07 if a register value changes (see the closure matrix and the H3 chain; PG3 even before H1 starts) -> 2. MD-01 and MD-02 (the pilot rules in the code) -> 3. MD-04 (FZ hash; needs your file list) -> 4. MD-06 (safe-stop) -> 5. (MD-03 already settled) -> 6. MD-07, MD-10, rest of MD-05 (confirmations) -> 7. MD-09 and MD-08 (needed after the pilot, not before). The FZ hash must be computed after items 2-6 are settled and before the first pilot call.

