## MD-01 SF counting for the pilot decision (C-04, C-05, C-31) — WORKING DECISION, formal entry needed
- **Decision/recommendation:** keep all flags; a call meeting SF2, SF3 or SF5 is one hard count; any other call meeting SF1 or SF4 is one soft call; `f_S` counts calls; **option B**: SF1/SF4 take precedence over SF2 (an empty body explained by an HTTP/transport error or by a block/no candidate is not also SF2); definitions D1-D8 (brief section 6.1); no new outcome label. Owner + advisor.
- **Consequences:** a 503/timeout/block with empty body is soft (tolerated up to `f_S` = 1); an empty body of a received non-error response stays SF2 (FAIL-S); hard flags are never hidden. **Alternatives rejected:** A1 (voids the `f_S` tolerance for adapter records, re-routes the round-1 action to the SF2 remedy), A2a (every empty block hard), A2b (hole for status-less records), per-flag `f_S` (protocol change).
- **Affects:** spec §13.4 (810), §13.6 (830-831, 838); `s10_scoring.py`, `s11_pilot.py`, `test_sf2_detection.py` (19), `test_sf_matrix_literal.py` (14), `test_sf2_variants.py` (11). **Prerequisite:** none.
- **Unresolved:** Q5 (candidate without text and finish reason vs no candidate; brief section 16) is NOT decided by this approval; it has its own box **Q5** in the Quick sign sheet; live provider behaviour is unknown.
- `[ ] APPROVE  [ ] REJECT  [ ] AMEND: ______  | Owner: ______  | Advisor: ______  | Date: ______`

## MD-02 Input-size basis, token measurement and cost (C-01, C-23, C-32) — WORKING DECISION, formal entry needed
- **Decision/recommendation:** preflight maximum **1,016 characters** per prompt (verified maximum of the build: 96 pilot / 1,248 main prompts; pre-filled in the authorization template, you confirm it when you sign the authorization); refuse an empty or longer prompt before any provider call; never truncate; characters are not tokens; `input_tokens_per_call_assumed` = 1,016 is the Step 7 ASSUMPTION, not a measurement; pilot: accept as is (C32-1); main run: measure by O4 after the pilot (brief section 17), O2 only with separate written authorization; US$100 ceiling unchanged, stop if it cannot be assured. Owner.
- **Consequences:** the hard-cap bound is about US$0.37 for 18 calls and US$51.88 for 2,496 slots at the 1,016 assumption; the input term is about 1.5 % of it. **Alternatives rejected:** inheriting the Step 7 bound silently; a gate on assumed tokens vs characters now (P3b: the form of a "measured basis" is undefined); a provider token count now (spending).
- **Affects:** `s10_runner.py`, `templates/owner_authorization_TEMPLATE.json`, `test_input_limit.py` (10); record 12.11 OD-10, 12.18 row 6. **Prerequisite:** none for the pilot. **Unresolved:** the main-run measurement itself (needs pilot data). Separate boxes: **Q9** (only if you want the assumed-token gate P3b) and **P12** (the read-only O4 script).
- `[ ] APPROVE  [ ] REJECT  [ ] AMEND: ______  | Owner: ______  | Date: ______`   Q7 accept C32-1 for the pilot `[ ]`  Q8 O4 first for the main run `[ ]`

## MD-04 FZ hash contract (C-03, C-18, C-19) — needs your file list (details in Appendix A)
- **Decision/recommendation:** the FZ hash = SHA-256 of a canonical index {path -> SHA-256} of the listed FZ files, computed ONCE before the first pilot call, stored as a new file, recorded in the decision record and every run manifest, recomputed by the tool (`verify`); enforcement by the gates needs the separate box **E-1**. **L-B (19 files, Appendix A) is a recommendation, not an adopted choice.** L-C (21 files) is possible only if you adopt, in the same entry, an explicit supplementary rule for H1-H4 fixes to the scoring and analysis files (draft wording in Appendix A, A-2). Owner + advisor.
- **Consequences:** any later change of a listed file changes the hash (new FZ version, re-pilot); the decision record, run folders and the final freeze manifest stay outside the index. **Alternatives rejected:** chain of existing manifest hashes; "researcher-supplied, unverified" (today).
- **Affects:** spec 797, 662, 1190; new `fz_index.py` (inactive P5, 7 tests); gate change in `s10_runner.py` (a separate approval). **Prerequisite:** the list, the A-2 answer and approval of the procedure; for the OFFICIAL hash additionally MD-01, MD-03, MD-05, MD-06, MD-07 and MD-10 settled and your instruction at that point.
- `[ ] APPROVE procedure  [ ] REJECT  [ ] AMEND: ______  | File list chosen: [ ] L-A  [ ] L-B  [ ] L-C  [ ] own: ______  | A-2: [ ] include [ ] exclude the Step 10 scoring files  | Owner: ______  | Date: ______`

## MD-06 Provider response safe-stop policy (C-12..C-15) — formal approval needed (details in Appendix B)
- **Decision/recommendation:** after the record is stored, stop for owner review on: (1) returned model ID missing or not exactly the requested ID; (2) finish reason not STOP, not token limit, not a documented block name; (4) record without HTTP status and without error marker; (5) error marker or non-2xx remains SF1. SF4 only for structural signals (no candidate; a block-reason field); block NAMES only after an authorized observation. Owner + advisor.
- **Consequence you must accept:** a stop ends the run as RUN_INCOMPLETE with no PASS/FAIL-S outcome, and `s11_pilot` refuses it; what that means for round accounting and the lineage depends on your answer to **B-1** ((a) it counts as a round, (b) it is void and re-run under the identical FZ, (c) MD-06 is not adopted); the options and their consequences are in Appendix B and the assistant does not choose. **Alternatives rejected:** record only (today); automatic SF classification of new names (protocol change).
- **Affects:** `s10_runner.py`, `s10_integrity.py`, 5 legacy tests; inactive P2 diff + 7 tests. **Prerequisite:** your answer to B-1.
- `[ ] APPROVE  [ ] REJECT  [ ] AMEND: ______  | B-1 answered: [ ] (a)  [ ] (b)  [ ] (c)  [ ] other: ______  | Owner: ______  | Advisor: ______  | Date: ______`

## MD-03 Kappa and the re-code procedure (C-02, C-09) — formal approval; touches frozen Step 7 files
- **Decision/recommendation:** K2: raw agreement + cross-tables per variable and Cohen's kappa labelled "intra-rater consistency; no inter-rater reliability claim"; "undefined" with counts for degenerate tables; sample = all if at most 20 else max(20, ceil 20 %); delay at least 14 days; concealed first-pass codes; columns `recode1_*`. Fallback K1 (raw only; a recorded departure from the literal spec line 1002). Owner + advisor.
- **Consequences:** K2 changes `step7/s7_recode.py` and codebook 5.1/5.3 = a Step 7 re-freeze before the FZ hash; K1 changes nothing. **Alternatives rejected:** K3 (needs a threshold no source gives), K4 (amends §16.3: protocol change).
- **Affects:** spec 1000-1003, OD-3, record 12.21 row 6, 12.24. **Timing consequence (verified in the code):** `step7/s7_recode.py` and the codebook are hashed by the Step 8 build manifest (`generator_code_sha256`), and the Step 9 evidence file names that manifest's SHA-256 (`s10_runner` gate line 139). K2 therefore means: Step 7 re-freeze (box **R-7**), a regenerated Step 8 manifest with a new hash, re-verification that the registry and checker bundle are byte-identical, and an evidence file created AFTER that. **Decide MD-03 before H3 is created**; a K2 chosen later makes the evidence file invalid and it must be recreated (a blind check on unchanged bundle bytes need not be redone only if those bytes are verified identical). K1 has no such effect. **Prerequisite:** decide before the FZ list is finalized and before H3.
